  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 PM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nMain impact this afternoon and evening isolated thunderstorm\ndevelopment in mainly the southern mountains once again. Areas\nof smoke still exist but not as significant and the air quality\nadvisory for Custer County has been discontinued. Hot conditions\ncontinue through Tuesday with low elevation highs remaining in \nthe 90s then a significant cooling trend sets in on Wednesday. \nBiggest impact in the long term is an upper level trof \napproaching with strong southwesterly flow ahead of it drawing \nin tons of moisture and have very high chances of precipitation \nas this trof moves through Thursday as well as Friday. Will be \nsome potential for flash flooding especially over recent burn \nscars should any of the heavier showers reach those. The chance \nfor showers and thunderstorms remain Saturday through next \nMonday but much lesser precipitation expected. Highs in the 60s \nmountains and 70s low elevations Thursday and Friday rising to \nthe 70s and 80s Saturday into next Monday.",
